## Agent rule — restart after edits

**Whenever you change stack component code, check if that process is running and restart it before ending the task.**

| You changed… | Typical paths | Process | How to restart |
|--------------|---------------|---------|----------------|
| **Master** | `master/src/**` | `cupidmq.exe` :9750–9752 | `cargo build --release` → kill → start with `cupidmq.conf` |
| **Producer** | `master/src/producer/**`, `master/examples/cupidmq-producer.rs` | `cupidmq-producer.exe` | rebuild example → kill → start again |
| **Consumer lib** | `python-client/cupidmq/**` | — | lib-only edits need no restart |
| **Consumer harness** | `python-client/harness/**` | `uv run python -m harness.consumer_cli` | kill python/uv → start |
| **Dashboard** | `dashboard/src/**` | Vite `:5175` | kill port → `npm run dev` |

**Common partial restart:** consumers only (test `max-batch-size-count`) — kill python/uv consumer, **do not** kill master/producers. After master-only restart, producers reconnect with new IDs.

**Windows — quick inspection:**

```powershell
Get-Process cupidmq, cupidmq-producer -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
Invoke-RestMethod http://127.0.0.1:9752/metrics | Select-Object producers_connected, consumers_connected, producers_busy, delivery_failures_total
Stop-Process -Name cupidmq, cupidmq-producer -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
```

**Makefile:** `make run` | `make producer-run` | `make consumer-run` | `make test-rust` | `make test-python` | `make dashboard` | `make publish`.

