## Architecture — control plane + P2P data plane

```
Producer(s)                         cupidmq master                    Consumer(s)
  │  TCP :9750 control                  │                                   │  TCP :9750 control
  │  PRDY / HBRP / DELV / FAIL          │  Matchmaker                       │  REG! → data addr
  │  ← ASGN                             │  ProducerRegistry                 │  CRDY
  │                                     │  ConsumerRegistry                 │
  │  TCP :976x data (P2P) ──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────►│  BATC listener
  │  BATC (keep-alive pool)             │  (payload does NOT pass master)   │  fetch ∥ process
  └─────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────┘
                                        │  HTTP :9752 /metrics
                                        ▼
                                 cupidmq-dashboard
```

**Master does not carry payload.** Match + metrics only. No persistence. BATC failure → producer **requeue** locally + `FAIL` to master.

Inner batch wire format: `[count u16 LE][len u32 LE][item]…` — master does not interpret item content.

---

## Match cycle (pull)

1. Producer local ring has items → **`PRDY`** to master
2. Consumer **`CRDY`** (max_items + tag) → opens BATC window after TCP ack
3. Matchmaker: CRDY queue (RR consumer) × PRDY pool (producer backlog ranking)
4. Master **`ASGN`** → producer (`data_addr`, max_items, tag)
5. Producer sends **`BATC`** on consumer data TCP → **`DELV`** after flush OK
6. TCP I/O failure → local requeue + **`FAIL`** to master → next match

**Critical CRDY order:** consumer sets `accept_batch=True` after CRDY sent (drain); master enqueues CRDY and calls `try_match` with no control-plane reply.

