## Python consumer harness (`python-client/`)

Two sockets:

| Socket | Role |
|--------|------|
| **:9750** | REG!, CRDY, PRDY, HBRP, ASGN, DELV, FAIL (control) |
| **:976x** | BATC keep-alive listener (`serve_batch_on_connection`) |

- Decoupled **fetch/process** (`prefetch_batch_count`)
- **`accept_batch`**: window per CRDY cycle; outside window → silent drop + `stale_batches`
- **`batch_timeout_secs`**: default 10s; stress uses **12s** (&gt; producer delivery 8s)
- **`data_idle_secs`**: default **60s** — close data TCP when idle (keep-alive)
- Optional chaos reconnect

---

## Ring (`src/ring/`)

Used on **producer locally** (`ByteRing`, `BatchAccumulator`). Cap → **drop oldest**. **`SharedRing`** exists in lib but **current master has no central ring** — aggregated backlog comes from producer heartbeats (`producer_backlog_*` in metrics).

