## Pitfalls (do not regress)

1. **Data plane delivery = TCP** — BATC + flush; requeue only on I/O failure; **`DELV`/`FAIL`** on control plane.
2. **`batch_timeout` consumer &gt; `delivery_timeout` producer** — otherwise consumer abandons cycle early.
3. **Bilateral keep-alive** — producer pool + consumer BATC loop; do not close TCP after 1 batch.
4. **Matcher only uses `Ready` producers in pool** — idle+backlog needs promote (HBRP/sync_ready_pool).
5. **`PRDY while busy`** — was no-op; now clears stale. Do not reintroduce silent ignore.
6. **Master-only restart** — producers reconnect; consumer data ports stay; partial restart desyncs IDs.
7. **Windows `uv run`** — 2 python processes per consumer (parent+child); normal.
8. **`std::sync::Mutex`** on producer writer — never `blocking_lock` Tokio mutex on async path.
9. **Inner batch format** — changes require aligning producer, consumer, and any batch-generating harness.

